Install and update (macOS)
--------------------------
Open the .dmg and drag BLiNX2.app to Applications, replacing the old one
for an update. The game files are inside the app. To uninstall, drag the app
to the Trash; your saves stay in Application Support.

The app is signed ad hoc on the Mac that built it, not notarized. On
another Mac, Gatekeeper may refuse it: right-click > Open once, or run
  xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/BLiNX2.app

Controls
--------
A controller works as player 1. The keyboard and the mouse work too,
merged with a pad on player 1, while the game window has the focus:

  W/S/A/D         move              mouse          look (right stick)
  I/K/J/L         look too          arrows         d-pad
  Space           A (jump)          left click, R  right trigger (sweep)
  right click, F  B (action)        E              X (time control)
  C Z             white, black      left Shift     left trigger
  Q               Y
  Tab             left stick click  middle click   right stick click
  Enter Escape    START (pause)     Backspace      BACK
  numpad 8/2/4/6  move too          left Alt       walk (hold)

Focusing the window grabs the mouse; F9 frees the cursor and grabs it
again. To change a key, put the control under [input.bindings] in
config/config.toml in the data folder, for example
  a = ["Space", "J"]
(config.default.toml beside the game lists every control and key);
keyboard = false or mouse = false under [input] there turns either off.
